    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and working. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Fix Summary\n\nThe bug was in how the `frai` CLI's `gate` command forwarded arguments to the `frai-gate` subprocess. The `--ci` flag wasn't being passed through properly because commander.js was parsing it as an option rather than including it in the variadic arguments array.\n\n### Changes Made\n\nI modified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 738-755):\n\n1. **Updated the action handler signature** to receive the `Command` object as a second parameter\n2. **Extract raw arguments from `process.argv`** instead of relying on commander's parsed args array\n3. **Pass the full argument list** to the frai-gate subprocess, ensuring flags like `--ci` are properly forwarded\n\nThe fix works by finding the 'gate' command index in `process.argv` and slicing everything after it, which preserves all the original command-line arguments and flags exactly as they were provided.\n\n### Testing\n\nI verified the fix works by running:\n```bash\nnode packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js gate init --ci\n```\n\nThis now correctly:\n- Creates `FRAI-SPEC.md` \u2713\n- Creates `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` \u2713\n\nThe package was rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build` and all test files have been cleaned up.",
